Oh, well. Here's the answer to all your woes. There's not much point
searching frantically to avoid possible trap-deaths when doing so 
is what's killing you through food depletion; and there's not much point
looking for secret doors unless you have reason to suspect there's
something to be found (and that is best done when all accessible areas
have been searched, since then it will be more clear what's missing).

When you enter a level it's got plenty of monsters (some of which will
become food); it may even have generated food items. Thereafter the rate
of replenishment is slower. Furthermore, if you descend, the monsters get
tougher - and in the early game, tougher monsters mean more nutrition.
You'd also have a better chance of finding those all-important first
daggers.
